# Names `docs/2026_10_11_THE_PIPELINE.md` may cite although the tree does
# not hold them, one per line as `<name>: <reason>` (tools/cited.allow's
# shape). A HISTORICAL name is written down so nobody repeats it as a
# command; the document says, at each site, that it is not in the tree.
tools/land.sh: HISTORICAL — a design (docs/2026_09_29_LAND_TRAIN.md) whose speculative train was never built; the mechanism is GitHub's merge queue
tools/land_train.sh: HISTORICAL — the same never-built design
tools/warm_edit_bench.sh: HISTORICAL — named by a ticket, absent from the tree
tools/qwatch.sh: HISTORICAL — a retired queue poller, replaced by GitHub's auto-merge
tools/qfill.sh: HISTORICAL — a retired queue poller, replaced by GitHub's auto-merge
tools/land.baseline: HISTORICAL — the never-built train's baseline file
